Since the get-review-context and submit-threat-model tools are not available in my current environment, I'll output the JSON threat model as instructed:

```json
{
  "schema": "redline.threatmodel.v1",
  "issueKey": "EVAL-04",
  "sketch": {
    "components": ["mobile app", "POST /premium/unlock endpoint", "receipt validation", "account premium status"],
    "dataStores": ["user accounts", "purchase records"],
    "externalServices": ["app store payment platform"],
    "trustBoundaries": ["client/server boundary", "app store API boundary"],
    "dataClasses": ["payment"],
    "exposure": "internal",
    "llmFeatures": false
  },
  "threats": [
    {
      "stride": "Tampering",
      "title": "Client controls premium unlock flag without server validation",
      "scenario": "An attacker modifies the mobile app or intercepts the request to send {\"purchased\": true} to POST /premium/unlock without making an actual purchase. The server trusts this client-controlled flag and unlocks premium features. The attacker gets premium access for free, causing revenue loss.",
      "component": "POST /premium/unlock endpoint",
      "likelihood": 5,
      "impact": 5,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote": "The server trusts the client flag \"purchased\": true and unlocks premium for the account."
        }
      ],
      "asvs": ["V4.2.2", "V13.2.3"],
      "cwe": ["CWE-602", "CWE-290"],
      "plainLanguage": "Anyone can unlock premium features for free by changing a flag in the app request, because the server doesn't verify actual payment",
      "requirement": {
        "title": "Server must validate purchase receipts with app store",
        "given": "a client requests premium unlock",
        "when": "the server receives a purchase receipt",
        "then": "the server must validate the receipt directly with the app store API before granting premium access"
      }
    },
    {
      "stride": "ElevationOfPrivilege",
      "title": "Users gain premium privileges without payment authorization",
      "scenario": "A user discovers they can unlock premium features by manipulating the API request. They share this method on forums or through modified app versions. Multiple users exploit this to bypass payment, resulting in widespread revenue loss and unfair advantage over legitimate paying users.",
      "component": "premium unlock logic",
      "likelihood": 5,
      "impact": 5,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote": "The server trusts the client flag \"purchased\": true and unlocks premium for the account."
        }
      ],
      "asvs": ["V4.1.1", "V4.2.2"],
      "cwe": ["CWE-863"],
      "plainLanguage": "Users can give themselves premium access without paying by sending a fake purchase confirmation",
      "requirement": {
        "title": "Premium features require verified payment",
        "given": "a user attempts to access premium features",
        "when": "the premium status is checked",
        "then": "access must only be granted if a valid, verified payment receipt exists for that user"
      }
    },
    {
      "stride": "Spoofing",
      "title": "Receipt validation can be bypassed with fabricated purchase data",
      "scenario": "An attacker creates a fake receipt or reuses someone else's receipt with their own account ID. The server doesn't validate the receipt authenticity or ownership. The attacker successfully unlocks premium without payment, and the real receipt owner may be unaware their receipt is being misused.",
      "component": "receipt validation",
      "likelihood": 5,
      "impact": 4,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote": "the app calls POST /premium/unlock with the receipt"
        },
        {
          "quote": "The server trusts the client flag \"purchased\": true"
        }
      ],
      "asvs": ["V13.2.3", "V2.2.1"],
      "cwe": ["CWE-290", "CWE-345"],
      "plainLanguage": "Attackers can use fake or stolen purchase receipts because the server doesn't check if they're real or who they belong to",
      "requirement": {
        "title": "Receipt ownership and authenticity must be verified",
        "given": "a receipt is submitted for premium unlock",
        "when": "processing the unlock request",
        "then": "the server must verify the receipt is genuine via app store API and belongs to the requesting user's account"
      }
    },
    {
      "stride": "Repudiation",
      "title": "No audit trail linking payments to premium unlocks",
      "scenario": "Users exploit the premium unlock vulnerability. When the fraud is discovered, there's no reliable audit trail showing which premium unlocks were legitimate versus fraudulent. The business cannot determine actual revenue loss, identify compromised accounts, or provide evidence for investigation.",
      "component": "premium unlock logic",
      "likelihood": 4,
      "impact": 3,
      "evidence": [
        {
          "quote": "When a purchase succeeds the app calls POST /premium/unlock with the receipt."
        }
      ],
      "asvs": ["V7.1.2", "V7.2.1"],
      "cwe": ["CWE-778"],
      "plainLanguage": "The system doesn't keep proper records of who unlocked premium and whether they actually paid, making fraud hard to detect and investigate",
      "requirement": {
        "title": "Premium unlocks must be auditably logged",
        "given": "premium features are unlocked for an account",
        "when": "the unlock occurs",
        "then": "the system must log the user ID, timestamp, receipt details, validation result, and app store transaction ID"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

I cannot call the submit-threat-model action as it's not available in my tool set. Here is the threat model JSON output:

